  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 719.03 Third-Party Laboratory Obligations",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 719.03 Third-Party Laboratory Obligations.\n\n(a) Before an O/O submits samples for analysis to meet monitoring requirements to a third-party laboratory, the O/O and third-party laboratory shall enter into a binding written agreement that requires the laboratory to submit all information required by, and as specified in, Env-Dw 719.05.\n\n(b) Each time an O/O submits any sample to a third-party laboratory for the purpose of meeting a monitoring requirement, the O/O shall inform the laboratory that the analyses being requested are to meet department monitoring requirements.\n\nSource. #9701, eff 5-1-10; ss by #12669, eff 1-1-19",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw700.html"
